    "verdict": "QR-05DJ (direction A, DET-native): record-dependent order growth — the direction T8 currently assumes away — does not achieve O7's manifoldlike emergence. Each element carries a record κ ∈ [0,1] and the relation probability is κ-dependent (p_ij = p0·φ(κ_i,κ_j)). At a matched 2-point ordering fraction the link fraction is only ≈ 0.38–0.71 of a sprinkle's, so the geometry-free record-driven law is not manifoldlike; and the 'sum' coupling leaks the record into the order (the κ–degree correlation ≈ 0.3), i.e. the order encodes the record. So record feedback trades manifoldlikeness for record-legibility: the more the order depends on the record (DET-native), the less it looks like a manifold (O7). O7's emergence is not achieved; the obstruction is a concrete higher-order statistic plus a covariance (record-leakage) cost. Track-B exploratory (Status M); no physical, metric, continuum, curvature or gravity claim."
